  <a href="https://tools.penumbraforge.com/lock" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--primary sl-launch-btn" id="btn-launch-lock">
    Open Secret Lock &rarr;
  </a>
  <p class="sl-launch-note">Opens on <strong>tools.penumbraforge.com</strong> — powered by Cloudflare Workers</p>
</div>

<hr class="sl-divider">

<div class="sl-how">
  <h2 class="sl-section-title">How it works</h2>
  <ol class="sl-steps">
    <li class="sl-step">
      <span class="sl-step-num">1</span>
      <div class="sl-step-body">
        <strong>Enter your secret and passphrase</strong>
        <p>Type or paste the text you want to protect, then choose a strong passphrase known only to you and your recipient.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="sl-step">
      <span class="sl-step-num">2</span>
      <div class="sl-step-body">
        <strong>Client-side encryption via AES-GCM</strong>
        <p>Your passphrase is fed through PBKDF2 (100,000 iterations, SHA-256) to derive a 256-bit key. The secret is then encrypted in your browser using AES-GCM with a random 96-bit IV. <em>The plaintext never reaches the server.</em></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="sl-step">
      <span class="sl-step-num">3</span>
      <div class="sl-step-body">
        <strong>Share the ciphertext</strong>
        <p>Copy the base64-encoded ciphertext and share it however you like — it's safe to transmit over any channel because it's meaningless without your passphrase.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="sl-step">
      <span class="sl-step-num">4</span>
      <div class="sl-step-body">
        <strong>Recipient decrypts with View Lock</strong>
        <p>Your recipient pastes the ciphertext into <a href="/tools/view-lock/">View Lock</a>, enters the passphrase, and recovers the original secret — again entirely in their browser.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</div>

